9398:</span>; it isolates the dilation step of the proof given there for Theorem&#160;<a href="sec-combining.html#thm:linearity">15.1</a>, namely the passage from the Fourier-square measurement to the exactly linear observables (<span class="ttfamily">references/nv-paper/fullpaper.tex:1099–1110</span>). Let \(\{ O(a)\} _{a \in \mathbb {F}_2^t}\) be binary observables on a finite-dimensional Hilbert space \(\mathcal{H}\), with characters \(\chi _u\) and Fourier coefficients \(\widehat{O}^u\) as in Lemma&#160;<a href="sec-combining.html#lem:boolean-fourier-transform">15.5</a>, and let \(\{ B^u = (\widehat{O}^u)^2\} _{u \in \mathbb {F}_2^t}\) be the Fourier-square measurement of Lemma&#160;<a href="sec-combining.html#lem:fourier-square-measurement">15.8</a>. Write \(\mathcal{H}' = \mathbb {C}^{\mathbb {F}_2^t \sqcup \{ \bot \} }\) for the auxiliary space of Lemma&#160;<a href="chap-projective.html#lem:naimark-helper">4.7</a> and \(\lvert \mathrm{anc} \rangle  = \lvert \bot  \rangle  \in \mathcal{H}'\) for its initial vector, so that \(\| \lvert \mathrm{anc} \rangle \|  = 1\) and \(\lvert \mathrm{anc} \rangle \langle \mathrm{anc} \rvert \) is the auxiliary projector of that lemma. Applying Lemma&#160;<a href="chap-projective.html#lem:naimark-helper">4.7</a> to \(\{ B^u\} \) yields projections \(\{ \hat{P}_a\} _{a \in \mathbb {F}_2^t \sqcup \{ \bot \} }\) on \(\mathcal{H}\otimes \mathcal{H}'\) with \(\sum _a \hat{P}_a \le \mathrm{Id}\) — a projective submeasurement, not a measurement — and such that, for every operator \(X\) on \(\mathcal{H}\) and every \(u \in \mathbb {F}_2^t\), </p>
9399-<div class="displaymath" id="a0000000925">
